WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.070
RICHARD BRANSON:<i> When
we found this beautiful island,</i>

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.406
<i>I really hoped that one day,
 I'd be able to work hard</i>

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:08.408
<i> and afford to come
 and live here.</i>

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:13.146
And then, finally, I thought,
"Okay, let's go and...

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:16.416
let's go and live
on Necker," and...

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.385
And not to retire,
on Necker,

00:00:19.451 --> 00:00:23.523
because I think I've maybe
worked even harder since then.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:28.895
<i> You can hear
 the lemurs.</i>

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.963
Yeah, calling
in the background.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.265
Which is, they...

00:00:33.332 --> 00:00:35.968
Yeah, it's a lovely sound
early in the morning.

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:39.505
(LEMURS CALLING)

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:40.507
Hello.

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:42.508
You're looking very wet.

00:00:42.841 --> 00:00:44.277
You're looking very wet.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.178
(CHUCKLES)

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:48.280
<i>Most of the animals we've got on
this island, we've reintroduced.</i>

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:51.184
<i> So, you know, there
 used to be scarlet ibis,</i>

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.085
<i>there used to be flamingos,</i>

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.354
<i> there used to be
 giant tortoises.</i>

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:58.357
<i> They were killed off,
 we've reintroduced them.</i>

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:00.560
<i> Giant iguanas, the same.</i>

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:03.463
<i> And then there are some
 species, like the lemur,</i>

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:05.898
<i> that, you know,
 weren't in this area,</i>

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.735
<i> but we're really
 delighted to have.</i>

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.104
<i> They just eat
 vegetables or leaves,</i>

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.641
<i> so there's no downside
effect to having them here.</i>

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:18.210
(CHUCKLES)

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.614
These two make love
every morning.

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:27.387
The male one just says,
all the time,

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:29.255
"What a guy,
what a guy, what a guy,"

00:01:29.321 --> 00:01:30.390
throughout the whole thing.

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.558
And then, when he
finishes making love,

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.626
he just goes...

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:34.527
(WHISTLES SHARPLY)

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.063
(CHUCKLING)
...and it's just, every time.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.432
SPEAKER:
Where did they get that from?

00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:41.601
I promise you,
it wasn't me.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.404
(CHUCKLING)
I don't know who it was from.

